    // IT THAT CATCHES THE PIXEL FOR IT (5.35: it is not the wire and shows nothing of itself; buildFenceWires lays
    // both). vC is the place on the wire's own line nearest the corner, vA.yzw the face's own outward normal.
    // WHAT WENT (polish3): the run was A FLAT UPRIGHT BAND 0.2 m broad with the wire painted down its middle, laid by
    // the metres across the band that each corner carried; what was drawn of the wire fell by the cosine of the sight
